{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Let us journey.</b> Some say it is the language of command, like \"Send the boy\" (Genesis 43:8), and likewise \"They have fallen upon us\" (Hosea 10:8)." "\"And let us go\": all of us, and I will walk before you; I will not turn aside from you. And it is possible that it is like \"And we journeyed from the river Ahava\" (Ezra 8:31) — \"let us journey,\" all of us, and I will walk before you:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:46:53.287303939Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}